e</b>

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:34.410
Are you not eating?

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:35.700
Allow me, then!

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:38.760
Oh, come on! If you eat like that,
 you're gonna get fat.

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:41.910
Still, the Derby...

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:44.260
You really are something, Teio.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:49.520
The derby is a once-in-a-lifetime race 
to determine the top horse girl...

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:55.430
I didn't have the luck to be involved, 
but I bet you end up the most popular.

00:11:57.930 --> 00:11:58.820
Hey!

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:00.970
What is it, Twin Turbo?

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:04.380
<b>T
w
i
n
 
T
u
r
b
o</b>

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:04.480
Well, you see, I got into 
Team Canopus, just like you, sis!

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:05.450
Really?

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:07.850
That means it's gonna be 
Canopus's time to shine now,

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:10.450
because it's got a big-shot 
rising star named Turbo!

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:11.660
You're declaring that about yourself?

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:14.170
Teio! I'm gonna beat you at the Derby!

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:16.670
I trained a whole bunch!

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:18.820
You can't even enter the Derby.

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:20.420
I can't?! For real?!

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:24.180
Then I'll win at the Kikkashou!

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:34.690
<b>races</b>

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:00.840
And there you are.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.300
Thanks!

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.300
<b>Japanese Derby</b>

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.960
The Japanese Derby is tomorrow, right?

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:05.680
Yeah!

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:08.200
I'm rooting for you to 
win the Derby, Teio-san!

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:11.010
<b>Gold
City</b>

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:11.010
<b>Hishi
Amazon</b>

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:09.960
Thank you so much!

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:17.770
I should drop by the shrine on my way home.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.020
McQueen?

00:13:24.020 --> 00:13:24.740
Oh?

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:26.790
Are you training on your own?

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:29.620
Yes, the Takarazuka Kinen is coming up.

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:30.870
Oh, right.

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:35.870
<b>I'm gonna become the number one horse girl in Japan!
—Special Week</b>

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:35.870
<b>I want to win the G1! —Mejiro Ryan</b>

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:41.840
The Derby is tomorrow.

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:42.870
Yep.

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:44.510
Are you nervous?

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:49.480
A little bit. It's the race I've been 
dreaming about since I was tiny.

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:53.140
Besides, you won the Tennoushou!

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:58.600
It'd be super lame if I lost 
after my rival won, right?

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:01.100
So I'm gonna win, no matter what!

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:02.420
See you!

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:07.560
Rivals...

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:17.550
Okay!

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:22.500
That's going on Umastagram.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.670
<b>Symboli Rudolf</b>

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:36.930
<b>Aim for an undefeated Triple Crown!!</b>

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:39.940
<b>Tokyo Racecourse</b>

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:43.080
The sports entertainment spectacle 
that captivates the entire nation,

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:44.440
the Twinkle Series.

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:48.700
I'm Akasaka on play-by-play, and 
on commentary we have Hosoe-san.

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:50.090
It's a pleasure to be here.

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:53.070
The main race of the day 
is the Japanese Derby!

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:56.330
<b>Japanese Derby</b>

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:56.330
An event so popular, 
the Tokyo Racecourse is at full capacity,

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:59.240
with some folks unlucky 
enough to be left outside.

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:59.580
<b>Admittance Limitations
 in Effect</b>

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:01.740
For the fans unable to 
make it here in person,

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:02.580
<b>Japanese Derby</b>

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:06.150
today's races are going to be 
broadcast live around the world.

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:06.460
<b>America</b>

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:10.300
And appearing last, in the eighth bracket, 
is the most popular girl in this race...

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:11.880
Tokai Teio!

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:19.690
Teio!

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:20.980
Teio!

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.910
No one in the eighth bracket 
has ever won before, have they?

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:26.900
Seriously?! That's bad news for Tokai Teio.

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:30.010
The fact that this course starts 
out with a curve so early

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:32.700
puts the girl in the eighth 
bracket at a disadvantage.

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:36.650
I think Teio's the one who will determine 
whether or not that's the case.

00:15:36.650 --> 00:15:38.750
Teio-san!

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:40.520
Good luck!

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:42.250
Thanks!

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:44.250
See ya!

00:15:44.490 --> 00:15:47.380
It doesn't seem like we need to worry.

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.190
You look ready to go!

00:15:56.190 --> 00:16:00.240
Yep! I'm looking forward to the 
victory concert after I win!

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:02.170
Someone's sure they're gonna win!

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:06.310
I'll be cheering for you, 
Teio... as your rival.

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:11.440
Okay, I'm off!

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:14.360
Good luck! You can do it! Yeah!

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:15.540
Let's do this!

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:19.730
The second most popular pick for this 
race, Rionatal, has arrived on the turf.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:23.830
Good luck!

00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:26.900
<i>This feels kind of like fate!</i>

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:30.020
The Triple-Crown horse girl Mister CB
 has pinned her hopes

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:32.720
on the third most popular horse girl, 
Cedar Blade, who has arrived on the field.

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:35.930
<b>M
i
s
t
e
r
 
C
B</b>

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:38.780
<i>This feels like it might 
be something like destiny.</i>

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:40.930
And next is the currently 
undefeated horse girl, Tokai Teio.

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:43.770
We are all eager to know if she'll
 be able to secure her second win

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:47.270
after the Satsukishou in her 
pursuit of the Triple Crown.

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:58.780
Wow, all of Team Rigil is 
present and accounted for.

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:03.090
The ace of our rival team is racing, 
so it benefits us to observe.

00:17:03.090 --> 00:17:05.500
We're rivals now? What an honor.

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:09.530
She might just make it happen.

00:17:09.530 --> 00:17:11.450
Winning the Triple Crown while undefeated?

00:17:11.450 --> 00:17:12.060
Yeah.

00:17:12.060 --> 00:17:14.640
There's nothing wrong with 
having lofty goals, but...

00:17:14.640 --> 00:17:16.520
But what, Hana-san?

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:17.740
Never mind.

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:28.770
<b>Japanese Derby</b>

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:35.700
The competitors are entering their brackets.

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:38.450
The horse girls are waiting 
at their gates, ready to go.

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:42.000
Last up is Tokai Teio, and she seems calm.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:44.370
She walks up to the gate with an 
expression that conveys confidence.

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:49.490
Winning this race, she would earn her second crown 
while undefeated after the Satsukishou,

00:17:49.490 --> 00:17:51.880
but will she be able to bring home the win?

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:57.100
As hopes and cheers are rising ever higher, 
and the Tokyo Yushun, the Japanese Derby...

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:00.030
has now begun!

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:01.390
Nice! That's a good start!

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:05.660
You should give her some 
pointers on her start.

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:06.600
Put a sock in it.

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:11.500
The horse girls are staying close to the 
center as they approach the first turn.

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:14.760
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven...

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:16.890
Tokai Teio is in eighth place, 
eighth place and on the outside

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:18.480
as they enter the first turn.

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:20.160
<i>Eighth place...</i>

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:24.290
<i>I'll have to run on the outside, 
but that'll let me get a feel for the others!</i>

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:25.580
<i>I can do this!</i>

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:28.620
Watch me, Prez!

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:32.440
Looks like starting on the outside 
hasn't been much of a problem.

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:37.970
Do you remember what you told 
Teio long ago, Maruzensky?

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:41.850
To be like Rudolf-chan, you're going 
to need talent, effort, and luck.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:44.410
And you can't afford to miss a single one.

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:45.640
Keep that in mind.

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:47.360
Yes, of course.

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:52.360
Teio's naturally flexible knees 
and ankles give her talent.

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:55.480
And she's put in more effort 
than anyone else, every day.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:58.010
That leaves luck.

00:18:58.010 --> 00:19:02.540
Well, they do say that the luckiest 
horse girls tend to win the Derby.

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:06.290
You could almost say today's 
race is a test of Teio's luck.

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:08.530
Teio-san...

00:19:10.070 --> 00:19:12.150
<i>They're approaching the third 
turn from the backstretch,</i>

00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:14.460
with Tokai Teio in seventh 
place on the outside.

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:17.400
Teio's being forced to run on the outside.

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:18.830
It's okay!

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:22.760
Don't you think that the outside is 
easier to run on in a straightaway?

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:24.970
There's no crowding, and the 
turf is in better shape.

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:27.560
She'll zip past them all in the last stretch!

00:19:28.570 --> 00:19:29.860
They're rounding the fourth turn!

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:32.440
Tokai Teio has moved up through 
sixth and fifth place!

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:39.820
<i>No one in front me. All right!</i>

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:40.530
<i>Whoa!</i>

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:44.490
<i>Tokai Teio, here I go!</i>

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.200
Tokai Teio is going hard in the last spurt!

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:49.840
Tokai Teio, moving up on the outside!
 She's climbing fast!

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:51.750
<i>I can't! {repeat as necessary}</i>

00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:54.240
With four hundred meters to go,
 Tokai Teio pushes through!

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:52.820
<i>I can't! {repeat as necessary}</i>

00:19:52.820 --> 00:19:53.710
<i>I can't! {repeat as necessary}</i>

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:55.340
She's made it to the top!

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:57.420
But there are other horse girls on her tail!

00:19:57.420 --> 00:19:58.770
Wow, impressive!

00:19:58.770 --> 00:20:00.920
She'll feel like she's flying now.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:02.160
And Tokai Teio breaks away!

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:03.440
Tokai Teio is clear!

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:04.930
Tokai Teio is still clear!

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:06.100
She's three lengths ahead! Now four!

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:08.390
There's no questioning it! Not anymore!

00:20:08.390 --> 00:20:10.150
Starting on the outside hasn't 
been any problem for her!

00:20:10.150 --> 00:20:12.110
Tokai Teio blazes onward!

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:11.810
Go!

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:16.260
And Tokai Teio... has won the Japanese Derby!

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:15.520
<b>Japanese Derby</b>

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:18.700
She obtains her Double Crown!

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:21.030
This was an absolute blowout!

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:24.290
Tokai Teio wins the Japanese Derby,

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:29.160
becoming the first undefeated Double 
Crown winner since Symboli Rudolf!

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.260
She did it!

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:39.210
Teio! Teio! Teio!{repeat as necessary}

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:41.210
And they're calling her name! 
The crowd is calling for Teio!

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:50.230
Teio! Teio! Teio!

00:20:56.600 --> 00:20:59.130
Teio might have just outdone the Emperor.

00:20:59.130 --> 00:21:01.440
I guess prodigies really do exist,
as frustrating as that might be.

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:06.650
Nicely done. Con—

00:21:05.920 --> 00:21:09.080
Save the congratulations for 
after she wins the Kikkasho.

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:12.220
She still hasn't accomplished 
her goal, after all.

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:30.370
It's time for the Winning Concert, 
where the brightest horse girls get to shine!

00:21:30.370 --> 00:21:34.130
And in the center position is the undefeated 
victor of the Derby, Tokai Teio!

00:21:34.130 --> 00:21:35.800
We might be looking at the first

00:21:35.800 --> 00:21:38.690
undefeated Triple Crown winner 
since Symboli Rudolf.

00:21:55.880 --> 00:22:00.880
<i>The impulse that races through 
me at the speed of light</i>

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:05.800
<i>is the determination to make my 
wish come true, no matter what it costs!</i>

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:07.760
<i>(No fear)</i>

00:22:06.790 --> 00:22:08.300
<i>It's once in a lifetime</i>

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:09.300
<i>(Trust you)</i>

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:10.800
<i>And in this moment</i>

00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:12.630
<i>I'm gonna bet it all</i>

00:22:12.630 --> 00:22:15.640
<i>Believing in myself!</i>

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:20.520
<i>If luck is what you really need sometimes</i>

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:27.720
<i>I'll find a way to make the 
melody of fate play my number</i>

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:34.810
Episode 1
 Tokai Teio
